n","created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T09:35:07Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-05T02:16:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T20:10:03Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112400","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112400","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112400.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112400.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This pull request implements support for Wavefront OBJ mesh files which include line and point primitives in their element lists ( e.g. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wavefront_.obj_file#Line_elements & https://paulbourke.net/dataformats/obj/obj_spec.pdf ).\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I also provide several miscellaneous improvements such as making read-only metadata properties un-delete-able from the editor resource inspection tab UI. Also, the rendering server will now explicitly report associated primitive types when meshes are dispatched with misconfigured indexing information. GLTF line loop modes are preliminarily supported by leveraging existing line strip support. Finally, the `MeshDataTool` class offers some initial manipulation capacity for working with any non-triangle-primitive mesh data so that users can at last at least query vertex and edge data from the surface array within a GDScript context.\r\n\r\nI used the following project to test these new features...\r\nhttps://github.com/PierceLBrooks/godot-mahjong-test","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112400/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112400/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}